SpecGate began in April 2026 as a customization of AgentSpec 4.2 and has since
diverged substantially. What descends from AgentSpec is the phase structure of
the workflow — the progression from specification through design to build, and
the practice of keeping phase artifacts as versioned documents in the
repository.

The following are additions developed independently and are not part of
AgentSpec:

  - The Verify Gate: acceptance as an executable command, with the six-state
    exit contract (0/2/3/4/5/64) and its runner, scripts/verify-gate.sh
  - The clarification protocol and its dedicated exit state
  - The graded release verdict (PASS / CONCERNS / FAIL / WAIVED) and the
    waiver taxonomy
  - The adversarial review contract and the advisor ledger
  - The EARS requirements grammar integration (the grammar itself is due to
    Alistair Mavin, Rolls-Royce, 2009 — https://alistairmavin.com/ears/)

AgentSpec remains actively maintained by its author as a separate project.
SpecGate is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or a fork of it in the git sense:
this repository was created clean-room, with no shared history.
